# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Luan G. F. dos Santos et al. (2025). Improving Bond Dissociations of Reactive Machine Learning Potentials through Physics-Constrained Data Augmentation.
#   Journal of Chemical Information and Modeling. doi:10.1021/acs.jcim.4c01847
#
# Version read: submittedVersion (sha256 61f01ca6e6245746...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 464 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/santos2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: three ANI models retrained with PCDA-Morse data
# (rigid bond scans labelled by a reference MLIP near equilibrium and by
# fitted Morse potentials elsewhere, with optional energy shifts to
# CCSD(T) bond dissociation energies) for 30 CHNO species, plus the
# ANI-1xnr reference model; force errors on the ANI-1xnr held-out test
# set. Bond dissociation energies, dissociation curves, combustion MD
# and rate constants are properties.

