###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - BDE RMSEs against CCSD(T) (ANI-1xnr 16.3, ANI-1xnr-M 16.7, ANI-1xnr-Mcc 3.6, ANI-Mcc 1.2 kcal/mol; Sec. 3) are errors of a derived property, not energy/force errors on configurations; not encoded as metrics.
# - Morse dataset sizes are approximate (~40k, ~35k, ~52k; Table 1); no n. The paper does not say whether the PCDA models start from the ANI-1xnr weights, so no base model is encoded; ANI-1xnr acts as a labelling teacher, which the paper likens to teacher-student training without calling it distillation.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/santos2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

